# DAC error-counter fix, part 1 of 2 (see dac_fix.md in this directory).
# Order vs part 2 is irrelevant (disjoint sites, stock-byte expects either way).
name: dac-fix-1-branch
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x03060d14
gate: build refuses unless the 2 stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: dac_write's success branch. Stock branches on a zero transfer
  result straight to the shared tail at 0x03060d1c, skipping the failure
  increment at 0x03060d16. The patch keeps the same condition and register
  state but detours through the reset trampoline at 0x03060d8e (part 2),
  which zeroes the DAC error counter (0x0300411e) so it counts
  consecutive failures instead of session-lifetime failures. Only the
  branch target changes; the second byte (0xd0) is identical.
expect: 02d0
replace: 3bd0
